/*!
    \class BindingProbe
    \inmodule HiddenFriendsReject
    \brief A two-parameter template class with an asymmetric hidden friend.

    The \a A and \a B parameters specify the key and value types.
*/

/*!
    \fn template <typename B, typename A> void bindingCheck(BindingProbe<B, A> &a, A key) noexcept

    Rejected positional-binding marker. Checks \a a using \a key.

    This command must not document the hidden friend. The leading
    declaration reuses the class's parameter names in reversed order, so
    the class argument still binds the same parameters positionally; but
    the key argument is spelled \c A, which the command's declaration
    binds to the class's second parameter, while the friend's key is its
    first parameter. Identical spellings with a changed positional
    binding describe a different function.
*/

/*!
    \fn template <typename L, typename R> void reorderedCheck(BindingProbe<R, L> &a, R key) noexcept

    Rejected reversed-class-arguments marker. Checks \a a using \a key.
*/
